// raft is how the members of one pkg/raft group reach each other and how an
// outside client reaches a group, beside the consensus transport itself (which
// is hashicorp/raft's own wire over a separate stream).
//
// ONE LISTENER PER GROUP. A host can be a member of many groups, each a
// namespace, and each answers on the package's protocol id with its namespace
// appended. The calls therefore carry no namespace: the stream already names
// the group.
//
// THE KV CALLS ARE THE GROUP'S OWN SURFACE. Set and Delete are applied by the
// leader; a follower that receives one forwards it there. Get is answered by
// whichever member is asked, after an optional barrier that makes the read
// reflect everything committed before it.
//
// THE REST ARE MEMBERSHIP AND HEALING. ExchangePeers gossips who has been
// seen, JoinVoter asks the leader to add the caller as a voter, and
// ClusterInfo, ExportFSM and HealAck are the split-brain healer's: compare
// views, take the winner's state, release the loser.
//
// ENCRYPTION IS NOT IN THE SCHEMA. A group configured with a key seals every
// message with it in the codec, so a request or a reply is never on the wire
// in the clear and a peer without the key cannot be understood at all.

